# Toolchain pins, read by CI and tests/stunt_lib.sh. This repository is tested
# on the current Aether release only: AE_PIN is that release, moved forward when
# a new one comes out, as the family's other repositories do. Nothing here
# proves an older release still works.
#
# History of the moves, for the reasons that still matter:
#
# 0.875.0 -> 0.923.0 (2026-11-19): contrib.quickjs from 0.915.0 (quickjs-ng
# 0.18) has no set_time_limit (an absolute per-runtime deadline, set_deadline_ns
# on now_ns's clock, replaced it) and its to_string returns (string, error);
# quickjs/ is ported to both.
# 0.923.0 -> 0.934.0 (2026-11-21): tracking moves. Aether #3799's preload fixes
# (openat2, renameat2, glob, fts_open wrapped; a refused dlopen always leaves a
# dlerror()) change a table only where a row used to die on them: Tcl's two
# dlopen rows, which now run in the contained child.
# 0.934.0 -> 0.935.0 (2026-11-22): a floor move. Every worker serves exports
# through std.guest's host-calls-guest verb (INVOKE, child.serve_exports), the
# QuickJS bridge is on contrib.quickjs's length-aware ABI (qjs_error_data and
# qjs_error_len, qjs_last_exception, qjs_set_poll_budget), and every bridge on
# the shared map's length-carrying C API and shm layout 2: all first in 0.935.0
# (aether PR #3802).
# 0.935.0 -> 0.936.0 (2026-11-22): a tracking move, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. Runtime ABI revision 6 (aether PR #3804) touches no bridge here:
# none reaches into std.tcp's private TcpSocket layout, and a table changes only
# where a row's behaviour changed.
# 0.936.0 -> 0.939.0 (2026-11-23): a tracking move, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. 0.939.0 removes std.http.client's process-wide connection pool;
# no bridge or worker here makes an HTTP request. A table changes only where a
# row's behaviour changed.
# 0.939.0 -> 0.941.0 (2026-11-24): a tracking move, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. 0.940.0 and 0.941.0 touch the HTTP client's retries and error
# wording, tcp.listen's backlog and actor message batching; no bridge or worker
# here uses std.http or std.tcp, and a table changes only where a row's behaviour
# changed. Factor's rows (the fork at FACTOR_FORK_REF) pass on both 0.939.0 and
# 0.941.0 (cachyos, GHL_REQUIRE_CHILD=1, about 2 minutes each, no row near its timeout).
# 0.941.0 -> 0.944.0 (2026-11-25): a tracking move, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. 0.942.0 to 0.944.0 are performance only: runtime actor batching (a
# batch from main waits for room in a full channel), std.math scalar functions
# inline, slice-view release inline. No bridge or worker here is affected, and no
# table row's behaviour changed.
# 0.944.0 -> 0.945.0 (2026-11-25): a tracking move, no new primitive needed and no
# source change. 0.945.0 fixes the macOS cross-build and three merge/typechecker
# cases (struct literal fields against module variables, a glob import binding
# only a module's exports, a local named like an imported function now E0301);
# the bridges and workers here hit none of them.
AE_PIN=0.945.0
# aeb is not used to build anything here yet; get.sh installs it with ae.
AEB_REF=v0.340
# The aether source ref stunt's catalogue is built from (stunt.c, stunt.h,
# stunt_main.c), kept at AE_PIN's tag. Release tarballs ship contrib/host/stunt
# without stunt.c and stunt_main.c, so the catalogue comes from the source at
# the release's tag: three files fetched and compiled with cc (no ae involved).
AETHER_STUNT_REF=v0.945.0

# Factor needs the embed-api fork of Factor (factor/README.md, "Caveat 1"): a
# distribution's Factor has no libfactor with factor_embed_eval. CI builds this
# repository at this commit (the one the tests were first run against, the
# tip of its feat/embed-api when factor/ was set up, 2026-11-05) and caches
# the build under the commit. Not a floor: any later commit of the fork that
# keeps vm/embed_api.cpp's entry points should do; bumped only in the commit
# that needs a newer one. Moved c467127bc2 to 6b88e3b758 (2026-11-21), the
# fork's branch embed-no-monitors, one commit on top: the embedded VM starts
# with -no-monitors, which ends the hang a refused directory listing caused
# (asks/factor-refused-opendir-hangs-since-0.927.md). The boot image below is
# unchanged: the fork's base is the same upstream commit.
FACTOR_FORK_REPO=https://github.com/aether-lang-dev/factor-language
FACTOR_FORK_REF=6b88e3b75828ffb6ce253cf7f1d665c15f369de2
# The stock boot image the fork's factor.image is bootstrapped from, kept in
# this repository and checked against its SHA-256, not fetched. It was fetched
# from downloads.factorcode.org/images/master/, which moves with Factor's master:
# on 2026-11-17 upstream's alist commit (705ad2d, "assocs: adding an alist
# type") changed the image, and bootstrapping the fork at FACTOR_FORK_REF
# (based on upstream 6221b7e, 2026-10-31) from it dies with "Memory protection
# fault at address 0x28" before the image is saved. This is the boot image that
# was current when the fork's tree was built by hand (2026-11-01), and it
# bootstraps the fork at FACTOR_FORK_REF (checked 2026-11-21, cachyos). Factor's
# own licence (BSD) covers it; its source is upstream's core/ at that time.
# It moves with FACTOR_FORK_REF: a fork commit rebased on a newer upstream needs
# the image that upstream's master built, which has to be copied in then.
FACTOR_BOOT_IMAGE=ci/factor/boot.unix-x86.64.image
FACTOR_BOOT_IMAGE_SHA256=02c331490d75a90cac175b4d88b3d8ef4df88e72bbf3ffe870bfaaa48f6e9ada

# Rexx is RexxAE, a Rexx engine written in Aether that lives in its own
# repository (rexx/README.md, "Where RexxAE comes from"). It has no release
# tags, so the tests take its source at this commit (tests/rexx_env.sh) and
# build its Aether binary library and its worker with the ae under test. Not a
# floor: it tracks RexxAE's main, as the family tracks Aether's latest
# release, and moves in a commit of its own that says what it brings.
# e7e9da6 (2026-11-21) is RexxAE's main when rexx/ was set up, targeting ae 0.933.0.
# Moved e7e9da6 -> 5c8862c (2026-11-21): RexxAE targets ae 0.934.0 (479c5b0),
# and TRANSLATE, VERIFY, STRIP and its cron parser are linear (0545b5f,
# 5c8862c), which rexx/containment/test_surface.sh's timing pass needs: they
# took 5 to 14 s per call on 1 MiB strings before.
# Moved 5c8862c -> 4e2ce73 (2026-11-22), RexxAE's main with guest-invoke merged
# (4c5426a) and its pin at ae 0.935.0: rexxae_call and the worker's EXPORTed
# labels, which the host-calls-guest tests (tests/test_invoke.sh) need.
# Moved 4e2ce73 -> 464e52c (2026-11-22): an object key holding U+0000 now
# crosses whole (c25b0ae; the map-nul cells), and RexxAE's catch-up with
# RexxJS 30fce5c (DATATYPE, SYMBOL, the data queue, array, JSON, URL and Base64
# functions, DO FOR/WHILE/UNTIL, JavaScript number text).
REXXAE_REPO=https://github.com/aether-lang-dev/RexxAE
REXXAE_REF=464e52c46bb8b2f0249d47572ba7532ef1c38442
